@startuml 3.9.2 - Downgrade Plan
title Sequence Diagram — 3.9.2 - Downgrade Plan

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

' === Participants ===
entity "Web dashboard" as webdashboard
boundary "SubscriptionController" as subscriptioncontroll
control "SubscriptionService" as subscriptionservice
entity "UserSubscriptionRepository" as usersubscriptionrepo
actor "USER (own account)" as userownaccount

' === Flow ===
subscriptionservice -> subscriptionservice: Validate account ownership, lower plan eligibility and workspace limit
userownaccount -> webdashboard: Select lower plan
webdashboard --> userownaccount: Show downgrade impact and date
userownaccount -> webdashboard: Confirm downgrade
webdashboard -> subscriptioncontroll: POST /api/v1/subscription/cancel
subscriptioncontroll -> subscriptionservice: cancel(user, command)
subscriptionservice -> usersubscriptionrepo: Load owned subscription and lower plan catalog
usersubscriptionrepo --> subscriptionservice: UserSubscription

loop invalid access / validation error / workspace limit exceeded
  subscriptionservice --> subscriptioncontroll: 400 Bad Request / 403 Forbidden / 409 Conflict
  subscriptioncontroll --> webdashboard: 400 Bad Request / 403 Forbidden / 409 Conflict
  webdashboard --> userownaccount: Display WORKSPACE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED or conflict error
end

subscriptionservice -> usersubscriptionrepo: Save downgraded plan / schedule change
usersubscriptionrepo --> subscriptionservice: writeOutcome

alt writeOutcome committed
  subscriptionservice --> subscriptioncontroll: 200 OK
  subscriptioncontroll --> webdashboard: 200 OK
  webdashboard --> userownaccount: Display downgrade confirmed
else write failed or version conflict
  subscriptionservice --> subscriptioncontroll: 409 Conflict / 500 Internal Server Error
  subscriptioncontroll --> webdashboard: 409 Conflict / 500 Internal Server Error
  webdashboard --> userownaccount: Display save error; retain previous values
end

@enduml
